       This is the only function that _m_u_s_t be defined by an auditing  library:
       it  performs  the  initial handshake between the dynamic linker and the
       auditing library.  When invoking  this  function,  the  dynamic  linker
       passes,  in _v_e_r_s_i_o_n, the highest version of the auditing interface that
       the linker supports.

       A typical implementation of this function simply returns  the  constant
       LLAAVV__CCUURRRREENNTT,  which  indicates the version of _<_l_i_n_k_._h_> that was used to
       build the audit module.  If the dynamic linker does  not  support  this
       version  of  the audit interface, it will refuse to activate this audit
       module.  If the function returns zero, the dynamic linker also does not
       activate this audit module.

       In order to enable backwards compatibility with older dynamic  linkers,
       an  audit module can examine the _v_e_r_s_i_o_n argument and return an earlier
       version than LLAAVV__CCUURRRREENNTT, assuming the module can adjust its  implemen‐
       tation  to  match the requirements of the previous version of the audit
       interface.  The llaa__vveerrssiioonn function should not return the value of _v_e_r_‐
       _s_i_o_n without further checks because it could correspond to an interface
       that does not match the _<_l_i_n_k_._h_> definitions used to  build  the  audit
       module.

